✅ Step 1 — Update system alternatives to point to Java 11

Run:

sudo update-alternatives --config java

You will see options like:

Selection    Path                                      Priority   Status
------------------------------------------------------------
* 1          /usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk-amd64/bin/java   2000    auto mode
  2          /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64/bin/java   1111    manual mode

Select option 2 → Java 11.

Then run:

sudo update-alternatives --config javac

Select the Java 11 compiler as well.

✅ Step 2 — Verify
java -version
javac -version
mvn -version

Expected:

Java version: 11.x.x
runtime: /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64
